desc: Beat Around the Bush Drum Replacer (mda BeatBox port) by chmaha
tags: drums drum-replacer trigger enhancer
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Drum replacer and enhancer. Three built-in drum sounds (hi-hat, kick and snare) are triggered by the
  incoming audio in three frequency ranges: the highs fire the hat, the lows the kick and the mids the snare,
  each with its own threshold and level. The kick and snare trigger filters can be tuned: for two seconds after
  you change one you hear the filtered signal ("key listen"), so you can set it to catch the drum you want.
  Hat Rate sets how fast the hat may retrigger, Dynamics passes the level changes of the input on to the drums
  and Thru Mix adds some of the input signal.
  Record replaces any of the three sounds with your own: choose Monitor, stop the source, pick a slot, play a
  single hit (recording starts with the first sound), stop again and go back to Monitor. The snare slot is the
  longest and records in stereo. As in the original, recorded sounds are not saved with the project.
  Ported from mda BeatBox by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects
  https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
